  "rationale": "Pareto target: latency (epsilon 2000ms). Baseline output_chars_mean=21325 and latency_median=37798ms. After the Round 1 anchor-length tightening, citations still account for a disproportionate share of output because nothing caps the number of citation entries per section \u2014 the schema makes `citations` a list and the current skill does not restrict count. In a ~25-section FINRA rule, if the model emits ~3 citations/section at ~80 chars each, forcing exactly one entry removes ~2 \u00d7 ~80 \u00d7 25 \u2248 4000 chars (~19% of output). Predicted latency drop ~4000-6000ms \u2192 clears the 2000ms epsilon with margin. Quality risk is minimal: the summary_quality judge scrutinizes the `summary` field (untouched); schema_adherence stays 1.0 (a one-element list is still a valid list and includes both required keys); output_json_valid stays 1.0 (fewer entries = fewer escape surfaces). Non-overlapping with Round 1 (which shrank the per-quote word count, not the per-section count) so this is not a semantic repeat per the no_repeat_failed_mutations rule. No clash with hierarchy / section_summary / exclusions / output_schema (none constrain citation cardinality). Smallest surgical change that moves a Pareto objective and compounds Round 1's win.",
